{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiNZBridgeScale","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiNZBridgeScale","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ObservableComplexVolumeVsFullPotential","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiKappaVsCkSign"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiNZBridgeScale.conventions_scale_ratio_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiNZBridgeScale.conventions_scale_ratio_two","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OhtsukiNZBridgeScale.lean#L100-L108","doc":"**Consequence 3: the two conventions demand bridge scales in ratio 2.**\n`κ_shape = 2·κ_pot`, so the full-potential convention's `‖c‖²` target is\nexactly half the complex-volume one — the A-binary IS a bridge-scale\nbinary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiNZBridgeScale.bridge_normSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiNZBridgeScale.bridge_normSq","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OhtsukiNZBridgeScale.lean#L90-L98","doc":"**Consequence 2: the bridge scale is locked to the normalization.**\n`κ_A²·‖c²‖ = (2πκ₁)²` (division-free): an independent pin of the bridge\nscale decides the A-binary, and conversely. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiNZBridgeScale.bridge_sq_re_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiNZBridgeScale.bridge_sq_re_zero","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OhtsukiNZBridgeScale.lean#L79-L88","doc":"**Consequence 1: the bridge ratio squared is purely imaginary** — the\nmatch forces `arg c ∈ {−π/4, 3π/4}`, i.e. the diagonal-ray geometry of\n`ModularRayDiagonalPrune`, derived rather than assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiNZBridgeScale.bridge_sq_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiNZBridgeScale.bridge_sq_mul","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OhtsukiNZBridgeScale.lean#L69-L77","doc":"Under the match, `κ_A·c² = −(i·2πκ₁)` (division-free form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiNZBridgeScale.OrderTwoMatch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OhtsukiNZBridgeScale.OrderTwoMatch","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OhtsukiNZBridgeScale.lean#L63-L67","doc":"The order-b² matching condition: under a linear bridge `u = c·b`, the NZ\nterm `i·κ_A·(c·b)² ` equals the Ohtsuki term `κ₁·2π·b²` for all `b` iff the\ncoefficients match. We take the coefficient identity as the hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0}]}